WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.190
What muscle memories do

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:02.500
we need to change in the

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.732
age of AI?

00:00:03.732 --> 00:00:05.012
I built some apps and

00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:06.222
websites for a few

00:00:06.222 --> 00:00:07.643
clients,

00:00:07.643 --> 00:00:08.943
for a small fee:

00:00:08.943 --> 00:00:11.213
brokers, restaurant

00:00:11.213 --> 00:00:13.059
owners, accountants.

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:14.600
I find myself building

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.269
the system under the

00:00:16.269 --> 00:00:17.460
assumption that

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.611
eventually

00:00:18.611 --> 00:00:19.871
this website and the

00:00:19.871 --> 00:00:21.441
systems will be used by

00:00:21.441 --> 00:00:23.230
multiple clients.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.270
For example, when I

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.774
design the API, I make

00:00:25.774 --> 00:00:26.754
sure they are very

00:00:26.754 --> 00:00:27.777
extendable.

00:00:27.777 --> 00:00:29.698
Basically, I was always

00:00:29.698 --> 00:00:31.448
building a SaaS as an

00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:32.570
assumption,

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.226
which is true for the

00:00:34.226 --> 00:00:35.826
last decade.

00:00:35.826 --> 00:00:36.956
But recently, I realized

00:00:36.956 --> 00:00:38.096
that this is not the case

00:00:38.096 --> 00:00:38.944
anymore.

00:00:38.944 --> 00:00:41.204
When the next restaurant

00:00:41.204 --> 00:00:43.905
owner, next broker, next

00:00:43.905 --> 00:00:45.305
accountant reach out to

00:00:45.305 --> 00:00:45.930
me,

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.632
I simply don't have to

00:00:47.632 --> 00:00:49.882
inject his or her data

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:51.622
into any existing system

00:00:51.622 --> 00:00:52.769
anymore.

00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:54.634
I don't have to reuse any

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.125
of the existing code.

00:00:56.125 --> 00:00:57.214
I can simply build a new

00:00:57.214 --> 00:00:58.067
one.

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.177
Because the cost of

00:00:59.177 --> 00:01:00.877
building something new is

00:01:00.877 --> 00:01:02.361
so low these days,

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:03.401
we can afford to build

00:01:03.401 --> 00:01:04.721
something from scratch

00:01:04.721 --> 00:01:05.738
very fast.

00:01:05.738 --> 00:01:07.228
We're talking about days,

00:01:07.228 --> 00:01:08.916
or maximum weeks, and

00:01:08.916 --> 00:01:10.256
then the new client will

00:01:10.256 --> 00:01:12.005
have a working system.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.573
And as a result, we can

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:14.993
hard-code a lot of things

00:01:14.993 --> 00:01:16.022
in the system,

00:01:16.022 --> 00:01:17.270
assuming that the

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:18.740
website, the app, the

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.703
system is only forever

00:01:20.703 --> 00:01:21.843
going to be used

00:01:21.843 --> 00:01:23.373
by one person, one

00:01:23.373 --> 00:01:25.435
business, one entity.

00:01:25.435 --> 00:01:27.005
So ask ourselves this

00:01:27.005 --> 00:01:29.161
question: in the age of

00:01:29.161 --> 00:01:29.950
AI,

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:30.980
what muscle memories do

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.520
we need to change?
